## Overview

Typing fast into the grid used to silently drop characters. With real
keyboard input from `page.keyboard.press()`, around 1 in 9 multi-digit
cells would persist only the second character (`A18` ended up holding
`8`, `A25` held `5`, and so on). Three race conditions in
`apps/web/src/grid/Grid.tsx` between the grid's keydown handler and the
inline editor's mount cycle have been closed, so 100 back-to-back
two-and-three-digit edits now round-trip correctly through the API
and survive a reload.

## Usage

There is nothing new to do — typing simply works at speed:

1. Open `/sheet/<any-id>` and click cell `A1`.
2. Type `1` `Enter` `2` `Enter` … all the way to `100` `Enter` as fast
   as the keyboard repeats.
3. Reload. Every cell `A1`..`A100` reads the value you typed.

The same regression test runs against the dev stack:

```bash
docker compose up --build -d
cd apps/web
npx playwright test e2e/fix-009-rapid-typing.spec.ts
```

It drives 100 cells with `page.keyboard.press()` and no inter-key
delays, asserts the rendered text for `A1`, `A10`, `A18`, `A100`,
checks every value via `GET /api/sheet/{id}`, then reloads and
re-checks.

## API / Interface

No public API changed. The fix is three behavior changes in
`apps/web/src/grid/Grid.tsx`:

**1. Printable key arriving while already editing** — append, don't
restart.

```tsx
default:
  if (PRINTABLE_CHAR_RE.test(e.key) && !e.ctrlKey && !e.metaKey && !e.altKey) {
    e.preventDefault();
    const state = useSheetStore.getState();
    if (state.editingCell) {
      // InlineEditor not yet focused (render transitioning) — append
      // rather than resetting to avoid dropping the first char.
      state.setEditValue(state.editValue + e.key);
    } else {
      state.startEdit(sc, e.key);
    }
  }
```

Previously the second key always called `startEdit(sc, e.key)`, which
overwrote `editValue` with just that one char.

**2. Enter arriving while `editingCell` is set** — commit and move
down instead of restarting the editor.

```tsx
case "Enter":
  e.preventDefault();
  if (useSheetStore.getState().editingCell) {
    // Input not yet focused (render transitioning): commit and move down.
    handleCommitMove(1, 0);
  } else {
    useSheetStore.getState().startEdit(sc);
  }
  break;
```

The earlier code fell through to `startEdit(sc)`, which reset
`editValue` to the (still empty) cell value. The next iteration's
digits then filled the wrong cell and produced a consistent off-by-one
across the run.

**3. `returnFocusToGrid` is now synchronous.**

```tsx
const returnFocusToGrid = useCallback((): void => {
  // Focus synchronously so keypresses arrive at the grid immediately after
  // commit/cancel — no setTimeout gap where keys fall to document.body.
  gridRef.current?.focus();
}, []);
```

The previous `setTimeout(() => gridRef.current?.focus(), 0)` left a
window where `document.body` had focus and any keypress in that
window was silently dropped.

`F2` was also tightened to skip its `startEdit` call when an editor is
already open, mirroring the new Enter handler.

