## Overview

Persistence (F-011) writes are debounced 500 ms after every commit, and
that timer was previously cleared on unmount with no flush. So typing
`42` in A1, pressing **Enter**, and reloading or closing the tab inside
that half-second silently lost the edit. `usePersistence` now registers
`pagehide` and `beforeunload` listeners that flush any pending cells via
`navigator.sendBeacon`, which the browser is required to deliver even as
the page tears down.

## Usage

Nothing for the user to do — the existing autosave just no longer drops
the trailing edit. Concrete repro that previously failed:

1. Open `/sheet/persist-close-test` and click `A1`.
2. Press **Enter**, type `42`, press **Enter** again to commit.
3. Reload the tab immediately (well under 500 ms after the commit).
4. After the reload, `A1` reads `42`. `GET /api/sheet/persist-close-test`
   returns `{"cells": {"A1": "42"}}`.

The regression test lives at `apps/web/e2e/fix-010-unload-persist.spec.ts`:

```bash
docker compose up --build -d
cd apps/web
npx playwright test e2e/fix-010-unload-persist.spec.ts
```

## API / Interface

No public API change — `usePersistence(sheetId)` is still a single hook
mounted by `SheetPage`. Two implementation additions in
`apps/web/src/hooks/usePersistence.ts`:

**1. A `hasPendingRef` flag** tracks whether the debounce timer is armed.
It flips `true` when the save effect schedules a `setTimeout`, and
`false` either when the timer fires or when the unload handler flushes.

```ts
hasPendingRef.current = true;
timerRef.current = setTimeout(() => {
  hasPendingRef.current = false;
  timerRef.current = null;
  /* …saveSheet(sheetId, obj) */
}, 500);
```

**2. A `pagehide` + `beforeunload` listener** flushes synchronously via
`sendBeacon` if (and only if) a save is pending:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  function flush(): void {
    if (!hasPendingRef.current) return;
    if (timerRef.current !== null) {
      clearTimeout(timerRef.current);
      timerRef.current = null;
    }
    hasPendingRef.current = false;
    const obj: Record<string, string> = {};
    cellsRef.current.forEach((v, k) => {
      obj[k] = v;
    });
    navigator.sendBeacon(
      `${API_BASE}/api/sheet/${sheetIdRef.current}`,
      new Blob([JSON.stringify({ cells: obj })], { type: "application/json" }),
    );
  }
  window.addEventListener("pagehide", flush);
  window.addEventListener("beforeunload", flush);
  return () => {
    window.removeEventListener("pagehide", flush);
    window.removeEventListener("beforeunload", flush);
  };
}, []);
```

`cellsRef` and `sheetIdRef` are kept in sync on every render so the
unload-time read is current. The listener is registered once for the
lifetime of the component (empty dep array) and the closure reads the
refs at call time. Both events are listened to because Safari fires
`pagehide` but not `beforeunload`, and dedup is provided by the
`hasPendingRef` guard — only one POST goes out even if both fire.

The beacon payload format matches the regular `saveSheet` POST body
(`{"cells": {…}}`), so the existing
`POST /api/sheet/{id}` endpoint handles it without change.

## Claims satisfied

- **VAL-FIX-010** — Entering `42` in `A1`, pressing **Enter**, and
  calling `window.location.reload()` inside the 500 ms debounce window
  leaves `A1` reading `42` after reload, and `GET /api/sheet/{id}`
  returns `{"cells": {"A1": "42"}}`.

## Limitations

- A SPA navigation that swaps `sheetId` *within* the debounce window is
  not flushed by the unload handler (the page is not unloading) and the
  hydrate effect's cleanup clears the timer without flushing. Not
  reachable in the current product because sheet switches go through a
  full reload, but tracked as a candidate follow-up fix.
- `sendBeacon` is fire-and-forget: a 4xx/5xx from the server during
  unload is invisible to the client. The next normal save will retry.

